cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  josim-cpr-bridge: a classical-to-quantum current-phase-relation
  bridge for exotic Josephson junctions
abstract: >-
  A bridge that carries an arbitrary Josephson current-phase relation (CPR)
  consistently from the classical superconducting-circuit simulator JoSIM to
  the quantum qubit spectrum. It mirrors JoSIM's supercurrent conventions and
  turns any CPR into a Josephson potential, a transmon Hamiltonian, and a
  spectrum (level structure, anharmonicity / Kerr, three-wave mixing, and a T1
  estimate), with a focus on non-conventional weak links such as graphene,
  twisted bilayer graphene, and high-transparency Dirac junctions.
type: software
